4. Arena's really interesting asset is the conditional evidence graph

The repo's preference model confirmed this.

It isn't trying to calculate:

Provider X = 91/100

globally.

ContextualBradleyTerry separates global skill from task-specific provider effects:

P(A > B | task)

and deliberately maintains separate models for:

blind/pre-price preference

vs

post-price economic preference

so price doesn't contaminate the quality model.

That means Arena can eventually know:

BigSearch

general search         91
breaking news          96
GitHub issues          61
obscure documentation  54


TinySearch

general search         73
