7. And Arena has an important feature Moltwork doesn't need: non-stationarity

This comes from the 402Pilot lineage.

The upstream problem is:

Service X used to be great
but changed model yesterday.

Service Y just dropped its price 80%.

Service Z became unreliable.

402Pilot's PA-DCT maintains separate quality and price beliefs per provider/task and discounts old evidence, explicitly so it can react to outages and price changes.

Arena inherits that mindset.

For Moltwork:

product_v37

is immutable/versioned.

If it changes, you can evaluate product_v38.

For an API:

POST provider.com/search

the identifier stays constant while its behaviour silently changes.

Arena's longitudinal evidence is therefore far more valuable.
