What I would do with Arena next

I would stop integrating it deeply into Moltwork for now and finish its actual scientific proof:

    Fix Hermes so its independent decision is actually parsed and used.

    Run the same scarce/full slates against real agents instead of synthetic personas.

    Run the 20,575-response 402Pilot replay.

    Add bad/mediocre/high-quality sponsored-provider negative controls.

    Fix/retire the simple retriever uncertainty bug and standardize on the posterior-based slate policy.

    Log exact slate/action propensities so the OPE machinery becomes meaningful.

    Make ArenaEvidenceV1 genuinely signed.

    Then demonstrate the killer claim: Arena routes x402 requests better per dollar than price-only, popularity-only, random exploration and 402Pilot alone, while discovering a previously unknown niche winner.

If you prove that, Arena has a very clean reason to exist even if Moltwork never existed.

And that is the strongest evidence that the two projects should stay distinct